cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use H2STAR, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "H2STAR: an open, uncertainty-aware materials-to-system model for sorbent-based hydrogen storage"
abstract: >-
  H2STAR translates the measurable adsorption properties of carbon sorbents into
  the system-level gravimetric and volumetric performance of a complete onboard
  hydrogen-storage tank, and inverts that translation to derive the
  material-property requirements implied by DOE system targets. It couples
  real-gas hydrogen thermodynamics, a modified Dubinin-Astakhov supercritical
  isotherm, tank inventory with a dual-bookkeeping invariant, vessel and system
  mass budgets, Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation and Sobol global sensitivity
  analysis, under pre-registered validation gates. Its central finding is
  methodological: the isotherm parameters are not identifiable from the
  single-temperature data the literature routinely publishes, so the defensible
  deliverable is an uncertainty-quantified acceptability region rather than a
  point prediction of the material requirement.
